<article class="env-proposition" id="51A3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/51A3">Proposition <span data-tag="51A3">7.1.3.14</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a topological space, $\calB $ a basis for the topology of $X$. Assume that $\calB $ is stable under finite intersections and that each element of $\calB $ is paracompact. For every continuous map of topological spaces $p: Y \rightarrow X$, the simplicial presheaf $\Sing _{X}(Y)$ of sections of $p$ is sheaf. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $F = \Sing _{X}(Y)$. We note that $F$ is a projectively fibrant simplicial presheaf on $\calB $. By Corollary <a href="/tag/BF18" data-tag="BF18">7.1.3.12</a>, it suffices to show that for every $U \in \calB $, every covering $\calU $ of $U$, and every linear ordering on $\calU $, the natural map $F(U) \rightarrow F(\calU )$ is a homotopy equivalence of simplicial sets. In other words, it suffices to show that composition with the projection $\pi : N_{\calU } \rightarrow U$ induces a homotopy equivalence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{/X}( U, Y ) \rightarrow \bHom _{/X}( |N_{\calU }|_{X}, Y) \]
</div>
    <p>
       of simplicial sets. This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/21FD" data-tag="21FD">7.1.3.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>